{"kind":"request","text":"Sign-in URL: add a browser as a device key for an existing person member, from the CLI or a chat session.\n\nToday a person who joined from the CLI cannot add a browser. Each device holds its own key, and an invitation is single-use. Membership has the act for this: `invite-key` with kind `device` opens a key for an active member (packages/platform/src/membership.ts:361). But `dap invite` issues only `invite-member` for people (packages/cli/src/commands.ts:879), and the page joins only a new-member link. This request depends on 355b0266 (the page admits membership@8). Order: after slice 9, or earlier when the builder waits on review. Not urgent.\n\nWorkflow to build:\n\n1. CLI: `dap signin [--minutes 10] [--open]`, run in the member's own DAP_HOME.\n   a. It signs `invite-key` for the member's own handle, with kind `device` and `inviteEnds` at most 60 minutes ahead (default 10). It uses the invitation credential of the membership version, as `dap invite` does.\n   b. It prints one URL: `https://\u003cservice\u003e/page/#/join/\u003clink\u003e`. The link is in the fragment, so the browser does not send it to the server, to logs or in a Referer.\n   c. With `--open`, it opens the URL in the default browser.\n   d. It waits, within a bound, for the matching `join` to be admitted, and prints the new key ID and the device kind. `dap signin --check` reads the result later.\n   e. The secret is kept only as `dap invite` keeps it now, and is never written to a log or an act.\n2. Page: route `#/join/\u003clink\u003e`.\n   a. The page reads the link, then removes the fragment from the address bar and the history (history.replaceState) before any other work.\n   b. It shows the room, the service, the handle and the expiry: \"Add this browser as a device for @hugh?\"\n   c. On confirm, it makes a non-extractable key in the browser, signs `join`, waits for admission, saves the connection and opens the room.\n   d. Expired, used, wrong-service and unknown-version links each show a plain refusal. The paste box on #/invitation keeps working.\n3. Chat: `dap mcp` gives the same as a tool. It returns the URL for the chat app to show as a link. The tool description says that the URL holds a single-use credential and expires in minutes.\n\nNot in this request: a member without `membership.invite` cannot add their own device. `invite-key` needs that grant (membership.ts:362). A rule that lets a member invite a device key for itself is a membership change for a later planner decision.\n\nTests: a CLI person joins, then `dap signin` adds a browser key on a native membership@8; the browser acts as the same member with the member's roles; the link is refused after use and after expiry; the page removes the fragment; `--check` reports the admitted key. Add a docs/cli.md entry and a docs/mcp.md tool entry.\n\nDone when the head is reviewed and landed. The planner redeploys dap-grow, and the owner adds a browser to @hugh in the grow demo with one command and one confirm. No deployment by the builder.","body":{"conditions":"dap signin issues a device invite-key for the member's own handle and prints or opens a fragment URL; the page joins from #/join, clears the fragment and confirms; a dap mcp tool returns the URL; tests on native membership@8; docs. After 355b0266; after slice 9 unless the builder waits. No builder deployment.","target":"inherit","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}